6 1113 #uuid "4ccca339-64f3-5137-9985-a212fbf787d1" 13194139535480 true] [17592186351386 1145 "Given a thin rod oriented along the  $x$-axis over the interval $a\\le x\\le b,$ if $\\lambda (x)$ denotes the mass density function of the rod, then the total mass of the rod is given by      \n\n$$\nm={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\lambda (x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x)=\\frac{8}{{x}^{3}},\\,a=1,\\,b=2.\n$$\n\nWe calculate the mass of the rod as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{8}{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}8{x}^{-3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[-4{x}^{-2}]}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & ={[-\\frac{4}{{x}^{2}}]}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =-(\\frac{4}{4}-\\frac{4}{1}) \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the mass of the rod is $3\\,\\text{kg}.$" 13194139535480 true] [17592186351387 1000 #edb/ref 17592186351388 13194139535480 true] [17592186351387 1000 #edb/ref 17592186351389 13194139535480 true] [17592186351387 1000 #edb/ref 17592186351390 13194139535480 true] [17592186351387 1000 #edb/ref 17592186351391 13194139535480 true] [17592186351387 1000 #edb/ref 17592186351392 13194139535480 true] [17592186351387 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535480 true] [17592186351387 1041 "selection" 13194139535480 true] [17592186351387 1104 #edb/ref 17592186351392 13194139535480 true] [17592186351387 1110 #uuid "349f921d-73c7-5ab0-ab4f-20aa5eca12cd" 13194139535480 true] [17592186351388 1034 "2\\,\\text{kg}" 13194139535480 true] [17592186351388 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535480 true] [17592186351388 1111 #uuid "b1bd2b04-4740-54f7-87dc-3308ef66e689" 13194139535480 true] [17592186351389 1034 "1\\,\\text{kg}" 13194139535480 true] [17592186351389 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535480 true] [17592186351389 1111 #uuid "f28bb641-56b2-53ea-82f3-37f5e46f2a7f" 13194139535480 true] [17592186351390 1034 "5\\,\\text{kg}" 13194139535480 true] [17592186351390 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535480 true] [17592186351390 1111 #uuid "b81