is the total mass of the rod?" 13194139535480 true] [17592186351400 1113 #uuid "33dc2ea2-d00c-5e39-945c-160ac13a087f" 13194139535480 true] [17592186351400 1145 "Given a thin rod oriented along the  $x$-axis over the interval $a\\le x\\le b,$ if $\\lambda (x)$ denotes the mass density function of the rod, then the total mass of the rod is given by      \n\n$$\nm={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\lambda (x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x)=2{x}^{3},\\,a=0,\\,b=2.\n$$\n\nWe calculate the mass of the rod as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}2{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{{x}^{4}}{2}]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{{2}^{4}}{2}-0 \\\\  & =8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the mass of the rod is $8\\,\\text{kg}.$" 13194139535480 true] [17592186351401 1000 #edb/ref 17592186351402 13194139535480 true] [17592186351401 1000 #edb/ref 17592186351403 13194139535480 true] [17592186351401 1000 #edb/ref 17592186351404 13194139535480 true] [17592186351401 1000 #edb/ref 17592186351405 13194139535480 true] [17592186351401 1000 #edb/ref 17592186351406 13194139535480 true] [17592186351401 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535480 true] [17592186351401 1041 "selection" 13194139535480 true] [17592186351401 1104 #edb/ref 17592186351402 13194139535480 true] [17592186351401 1110 #uuid "d3bff5ee-5c71-5a68-adf4-816454d0d3fb" 13194139535480 true] [17592186351402 1034 "8\\,\\text{kg}" 13194139535480 true] [17592186351402 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535480 true] [17592186351402 1111 #uuid "46a13283-a80d-5f5f-be82-25bfa0680244" 13194139535480 true] [17592186351403 1034 "12\\,\\text{kg}" 13194139535480 true] [17592186351403 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535480 true] [17592186351403 1111 #uuid "5e0662a7-dccd-5c84-83f6-c0b4f5367a1e" 13194139535480 true] [17592186351404 1034 "10\\,\\text{kg}" 13194139535480 true] [17592186351404 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535480 true] [17592186351404 1111 #uuid "227f31b3-e1b2-57d8-8e41-7ea14a125c6c" 13194139535480 true] [17592186351405 1034 "6\\,\\text{kg}" 13194139535480 true] [17592186351405 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535480 true] [17592186351405 1111 #uuid "f7e3a1e3-a2da-51af-bc03-3d0db677f0e8" 13194139535480 true] [17592186351406 1034 "4\\,\\text{kg}" 13194139535480 true] [17592186351406 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535480 true] [17592186351406 1111 #uuid "5051d321-4cea-5b3f-b9e2-0a6073c7e6bf" 13194139535480 true] [17592186351407 1017 #edb/ref 17592186351408 13194139535480 true] [17592186351407 1089 "q-163036" 13194139535480 true] [17592186351407 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535480 true] [17592186351407 1100 "A thin rod with mass density function $\\lambda (x)=6x,$ measured in $\\text{kg/m},$ is placed along the $x$-axis over the interval $1\\le x\\le 2,$ where $x$ is measured in meters. Find the moment of the rod about the origin." 13194139535480 true] [17592186351407 1113 #uuid "1f5ebe42-9a69-55b4-85c3-da9b0cecac83" 13194139535480 true] [17592186351407 1145 "The moment about the origin $O$ of a rod with mass density function $\\lambda (x)$ for $a\\le x\\le b$ is given by \n\n$$\n{M}_{O}={\\int }_{a}^{b}x\\,\\lambda (x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x)=6x,\\,a=1,\\,b=2.\n$$\n\nWe calculate the moment of the rod about the origin as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{O} & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}x\\cdot 6x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}6{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[2{x}^{3}]}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =2\\cdot ({2}^{3}-{1}^{3}) \\\\  & =14\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the required moment is $14\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}.$" 13194139535480 true] [17592186351408 1000 #edb/ref 17592186351409 13194139535480 true] [17592186351408 1000 #edb/ref 17592186351410 13194139535480 true] [17592186351408 1000 #edb/ref 17592186351411 13194139535480 true] [17592186351408 1000 #edb/ref 17592186351412 13194139535480 true] [17592186351408 1000 #edb/ref 17592186351413 13194139535480 true] [17592186351408 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535480 true] [17592186351408 1041 "selection" 13194139535480 true] [17592186351408 1104 #edb/ref 17592186351413 13194139535480 true] [17592186351408 1110 #uuid "735e2c7f-3a8c-564a-b6a9-508b924dd3ab" 13194139535480 true] [17592186351409 1034 "16\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" 13194139535480 true] [17592186351409 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535480 true] [17592186351409 1111 #uuid "2c93a7a6-90fb-5930-b090-ce19a9936965" 13194139535480 true] [17592186351410 1034 "12\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" 13194139535480 true] [17592186351410 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535480 true] [17592186351410 1111 #uuid "93871334-7775-52a4-aed7-3c5f84b07edb" 13194139535480 true] [17592186351411 1034 "7\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" 13194139535480 true] [17592186351411 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535480 true] [17592186351411 1111 #uuid "61eb5ea7-4724-5d42-b74f-ac12f085d3bb" 13194139535480 true] [17592186351412 1034 "9\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" 13194139535480 true] [17592186351412 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535480 true] [17592186351412 1111 #uuid "0037044b-3072-527e-8ac2-1b376f743163" 13194139535480 true] [17592186351413 1034 "14\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" 13194139535480 true] [17592186351413 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535480 true] [17592186351413 1111 #uuid "7df42914-ac94-5d0b-a1c3-856170711096" 13194139535480 true] [17592186351414 1017 #edb/ref 17592186351415 13194139535480 true] [17592186351414 1089 "q-163039" 13194139535480 true] [17592186351414 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535480 true] [17592186351414 1100 "A thin rod with mass density function $\\lambda (x)=3x+1,$ measured in $\\text{kg/m},$ is placed along the $x$-axis over the interval $1\\le x\\le 2,$ where $x$ is measured in meters. Find the moment of the rod about the origin." 13194139535480 true] [17592186351414 1113 #uuid "d2c0bfdd-0747-5e9c-ade1-1661720da9c8" 13194139535480 true] [17592186351414 1145 "The moment about the origin $O$ of a rod with mass density function $\\lambda (x)$ for $a\\le x\\le b$ is given by \n\n$$\n{M}_{O}={\\int }_{a}^{b}x\\,\\lambda (x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x)=3x+1,\\,a=1,\\,b=2.\n$$\n\nWe calculate the moment of the rod about the origin as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{O} & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}x\\cdot (3x+1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}3{x}^{2}+x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[{x}^{3}+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}]}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =(8+\\frac{4}{2})-(1+\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{17}{2} \\\\  & =8.5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the required moment is $8.5\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}.$" 13194139535480 true] [17592186351415 1000 #edb/ref 17592186351416 13194139535480 true] [17592186351415 1000 #edb/ref 17592186351417 13194139535480 true] [17592186351415 1000 #edb/ref 17592186351418 13194139535480 true] [17592186351415 1000 #edb/ref 17592186351419 13194139535480 true] [17592186351415 1000 #edb/ref 17592186351420 13194139535480 true] [17592186351415 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535480 true] [17592186351415 1041 "selection" 13194139535480 true] [17592186351415 1104 #edb/ref 17592186351416 13194139535480 true] [17592186351415 1110 #uuid "fa5b343b-f410-5840-a849-0c64eb6a7b73" 13194139535480 true] [17592186351416 1034 "8.5\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" 13194139535480 true] [17592186351416 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535480 true] [17592186351416 1111 #uuid "12bf9c26-f0e3-5951-a5e8-e9f8033e8147" 13194139535480 true] [17592186351417 1034 "10\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" 13194139535480 true] [17592186351417 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535480 true] [17592186351417 1111 #uuid "89436c32-92c9-5406-ad2d-4a625a0d3835" 13194139535480 true] [17592186351418 1034 "7\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" 13194139535480 true] [17592186351418 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535480 true] [17592186351418 1111 #uuid "e08ece88-bbe1-5197-859b-2bb1d4ed0ccd" 13194139535480 true] [17592186351419 1034 "9\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" 13194139535480 true]